Package: fereg
Title: Fast Fixed-Effects Estimation with the 'fixest' Interface
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Leo", "Liu", email = "auleo.liu@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Authors of the dependency Rust crates", role = "ctb",
           comment = "see inst/AUTHORS")
  )
Description: OLS, instrumental-variables (2SLS), Poisson and logit regressions
    with any number of high-dimensional fixed effects, interactions of fixed
    effects, varying slopes, weights and iid, heteroskedasticity-robust or
    multiway-clustered standard errors. The formula syntax, arguments, results
    and methods follow the 'fixest' package and reproduce its estimates. The
    computations run in a parallel Rust library that eliminates the largest
    fixed effect exactly and solves for the others by preconditioned conjugate
    gradient.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
